eq 0$ iff $ inom{n}{k} 
eq 0$ (always true for valid compositions) AND $p_i 
eq 0$ whenever $k_i 
eq 0$. The condition '$p_i 
eq 0$ whenever $k_i 
eq 0$' is equivalent to the product $\prod_i p_i^{k_i} 
eq 0$ in $\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^\infty$, since $0^0 = 1$ (vacuously nonzero) and $p_i^{k_i} = 0$ iff $p_i = 0$ and $k_i > 0$.
